From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:07:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Nightly enrichment: a run cut off by a restart is closed, and
 resumed early in its night

16 Oct: the 01:00 incremental run was killed by the 01:24 deploy. Its row
read "running" with nothing processed until morning, and nothing ran
again until the next night; 17 older rows were left behind the same way.

At boot a "running" row can only belong to the process before, so it is
closed as failed with "cut off by a restart". An incremental run cut off
the same UTC night before 03:00 starts again; later than that, a resumed
run (about three hours, capped) would reach the day's testing, so it
waits for the next night.

